        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f6715ff2-2c0f-545d-a060-55dcb7d1c04b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Cressida Cowell, Neal Layton\n- Companies: DreamWorks Animation\n- Products: How to Train Your Dragon franchise, Legend of the Boneknapper Dragon, Book of Dragons, Gift of the Night Fury, Dawn of the Dragon Racers, That Rabbit Belongs to Emily Brown\n- Topics: children's literature, animated short films\n\nFacts:\n- In 2006, Cressida Cowell wrote the children's picture book That Rabbit Belongs to Emily Brown, and Neal Layton illustrated it.\n- In 2010, DreamWorks Animation released Legend of the Boneknapper Dragon, an animated short film that served as a sequel to How to Train Your Dragon.\n- In 2010, the How to Train Your Dragon franchise included the short film Legend of the Boneknapper Dragon.\n- In 2011, the How to Train Your Dragon franchise included the short films Book of Dragons and Gift of the Night Fury.\n- In 2014, the How to Train Your Dragon franchise included the short film Dawn of the Dragon Racers.\n- Cressida Cowell, born on 15 April 1966, is an English children's author known for the How to Train Your Dragon novel series.\n- DreamWorks Animation adapted Cressida Cowell's How to Train Your Dragon novels into an award-winning screen franchise.",
